  "narrative": "The new screen mostly rejects the registered directions, but it yields one strong post-hoc signal and one borderline promising registered signal. Applying the 10% relative-difference rule, the clinically meaningful absolute threshold is about 0.0093 for outcome_006 and outcome_014 (means near -0.093) and about 0.0269 for outcome_013 (mean near -0.269). H29 is the best registered positive candidate: feature_023 presence associated with weaker dependency for outcome_006 has signed estimate +0.0458, about five times threshold, but its interval [-0.0023, +0.0939] still includes zero and clinically negligible values. H30 provides same-direction support for outcome_014, +0.0355 [-0.0123, +0.0833], also above threshold but imprecise. Because these are cross-outcome consistent for the same predictor and outcome-specific enough to justify follow-up, I validate H29 rather than H3 or H30. If H29 independently clears the clinical threshold, the feature_023 path becomes a much stronger association; if it fails like H8/H31, both H29 and H30 should be closed or heavily deprioritized.\n\nThe new large surprise is H38: for outcome_014, feature_027=1 versus 0 under the registered vulnerability direction -1 gives signed estimate -0.796 with a very tight interval [-0.816, -0.776]. This is enormous and excludes zero, but it is opposite the pre-registered vulnerability direction: it implies feature_027 presence is associated with far weaker dependency/higher outcome_014 score. The original H38 claim must be rejected because it tested the wrong direction, but the magnitude is too large to discard as noise without a post-hoc follow-up. I therefore keep the original claim active and register a reversal proposal with direction +1, parent H38, to evaluate whether feature_027 is an outcome_014-specific resistance/weaker-dependency marker. I do not treat this as accepted yet; it is a post-hoc reversal after seeing the data and needs at least explicit follow-up, and possibly later independent validation. It could also reflect coding/leakage or an outcome-specific artifact, so causal or biological interpretation is not supported from this single comparison.\n\nMost other new predictors are not compelling after multiplicity and cross-outcome consistency checks. H19 for feature_030 on outcome_013 is below the outcome_013 threshold and crosses zero; H20 for feature_023 on outcome_013 is opposite and below threshold, so I reject the outcome_013 claim even while the low-threshold H29/H30 feature_023 signals remain active. H27/H28 show no feature_030 vulnerability association. feature_050, feature_037, and feature_027 original vulnerability paths are inconsistent across outcome_006/outcome_014 or only borderline, so those original claims are rejected/closed, except for the H38 post-hoc reversal. H3 remains unresolved and potentially valuable but is currently less promising than H29/H30 and H38-reversed. All conclusions are dataset-level associations; none should be interpreted causally or as broadly generalizable without independent validation and cross-predictor/cross-outcome consistency.",
  "research_notes": "Round 3 appraise update. No accepted claims yet. Clinical absolute thresholds used: outcome_006/outcome_014 ≈0.0093; outcome_013 ≈0.0269; outcome_012 ≈0.0248. Closed/deprioritized paths: feature_030, feature_050, feature_037; feature_027 original vulnerability direction; feature_023 outcome_013 specific claim. Active candidates: H3 (feature_060 main effect outcome_006, lower priority), H29/H30 feature_023 weaker-dependency direction on outcome_006/outcome_014, and post-hoc reversed feature_027 on outcome_014 (new proposal parent H38). Validation requested: H29 because it is the strongest registered positive signal with cross-outcome support; independent interval will decide whether to accept or close the feature_023 path. H38 has huge opposite evidence [-0.816,-0.776] under direction -1; original H38 rejected, but reversed proposal registered. If reversed claim analysis reuses same data and gives tight +0.796 interval, consider accepting as dataset association only if leakage/coding concerns are acknowledged, or request validation for the reversed claim next iteration. Do not over-interpret H38 as causal or generalizable; it may be outcome_014-specific artifact. Continue avoiding constants, ID-like/rare features, and already-refuted predictor paths unless clearly refined."
